# Port Plan — Step 12: Context Management (Ruby → Python)

Port the step-12 delta: real context-window tracking, a colour-coded usage
indicator, auto-compaction, a second per-turn circuit breaker, normalized
reasoning blocks, and the OpenAI Responses API move.

> **This one is a pure forward delta, not a merge.** Ruby's step 12 was a
> genuine two-way merge — that snapshot had been branched before the MCP host
> and the tasks layer, so half the work was carrying steps 10–11 into it
> (`docs/plans/step_deltas/12_context`). **None of that applies here.**
> `week1_baseline/python/12_context` is a verbatim copy of `python/11_tui`
> (`diff -rq --exclude=__pycache__` empty, confirmed 2026-08-04), and `11_tui`
> already carries the MCP host, `tasks/`, and the response cost metadata. The
> Python side inherits the merged result and only has to add step 12 itself.

The four judgment calls that merge forced are **already settled** (§3). Adopt
them; do not re-open them here.

